<h2>The Brief</h2>
<p>A classic Santa Barbara ranch home with a cathedral wood-beam ceiling, skylights, and a garden greenhouse window deserved a kitchen that respected the architecture without imitating it. Gillian Amery's answer: bring German engineering into the room, but in a wood tone and profile that makes the cabinetry feel like it <em>belongs</em> under those beams — not like it was flown in from a downtown showroom.</p>
<p>The result is a kitchen that reads immediately as warm, calm, and architectural. Clients see it and feel it before they can tell you why it works.</p>

